fresh-eyes: agent review of the fixture identity fix. Scope: the test fixture repo carries user.name and user.email in its local config, so edit_reference reflog writes stop depending on the machine's global gitconfig. An independent reviewer confirmed the appended ini is valid against gix's serializer, that isolated reopens still load repo-local config, and that no test asserts on committer identity. Mutation: without the fixture identity, git::tests::a_real_repository_round_trips_through_the_cache and git::tests::tags_and_a_detached_head_mirror_into_the_slot go red with MissingCommitter on a host without a global gitconfig (reproduced in a debian container); with it, 198 lib tests pass there.
